agent-ops task task-64fd0753-5be6-438c-989d-c7337d4fe2d1: Recover native final proof without repeating a passed primary review
intent: Implement bounded native coordinator final-proof recovery with durable exact-bound primary-review checkpoints and shared retry accounting, preserving valid machine evidence, all existing authority/identity checks and complete paired review/receipt proof. Keep standalone CLI and child handoff unchanged.
criteria:
- primary-checkpoint: In a native coordinator final proof a primary PASS is durably checkpointed after the source recheck and before the adversarial round; resuming the same exact-bound review makes no second primary call, keeps the original primary session and uses a new adversarial session distinct from the primary and any interrupted one, the attestation primaryReportDigest equals the checkpoint report digest, a saved complete pair is reconstructed without any model call, and a refuted pair is never resumed.
- automatic-final-recovery: Native coordinator finalization persists a pending final-proof intent before the proof step; a replayable interruption found inline or pending at supervisor restart reruns the proof once before any writer starts, with no target/ref mutation or receipt before the full existing gate passes; task advance skips verify only when current passing evidence holds for the candidate, re-verifies missing or stale evidence, and stops on FAIL/UNKNOWN without review.
- bounded-retry: Inside native final proof the reviewer in-process retry is disabled and the supervisor's single recovery is the only automatic retry per immutable attempt key (candidate, target, contract, policy config and runtime); concurrent settles, restart and repeated finalization of the same key cannot reset or exceed 1/1; once stopped, run state finalProof (recoveries, first and last failures, stopped) and run status ('Final proof recovery: n/1 used; first failure ...; last failure ...; automatic recovery stopped') show it.
- identity-and-authority: Automatic replay is refused, with a RUN_FINAL_PROOF_RECOVERY_STOPPED event, and the existing repair path keeps the checkout with its uncommitted content untouched when the coordinator checkout is dirty, the attempt key changed, the run is stopped or not active, an integration exists, any process of the old proof group remains in the process table, the failure is non-replayable (substantive FAIL, UNKNOWN, timeout, overflow, non-transient NOT_RUN) or the checkpoint is corrupt (review NOT_RUN checkpoint-invalid); no path turns FAIL or a partial result into PASS.
- compatibility-and-evidence: Run states without final-proof data stay readable and behave as before; standalone review and batch keep their in-process retry and never read or write checkpoints; a review outside the registered native proof process, including one with a forged AGENT_OPS_RUN_ID, gets no checkpoint journal; child handoff, target-move retry and sealed integration recovery keep their existing behavior.
